# Circuit shape of `pedersen128_hash_uncompressed` for each operand mode, input length and a fixed set of inputs.
# Line: <type.mode of each operand> | <value of each constant operand, _ for a variable one, or *> : <result>
# A `_` stands for each value of a variable operand. The test checks that they give one result.
# Result: constants public private constraints nonzeros(A/B/C) output-mode digest, or halt.
# The digest is the first 64 bits of a SHA-256 hash of the constraint structure: the order of the constraints, and the constant,
# coefficients and variables of each linear combination.
# A mixed output mode counts the constant, public and private bits.
# The test also checks each case with the console operation. A defined case must give the console
# value in a satisfied circuit. An undefined case must halt or leave the circuit unsatisfied.
# A `*` line gives the result of each case of its block that has no line of its own.
# Regenerate: UPDATE_CIRCUIT_SNAPSHOTS=1 cargo test -p snarkvm-circuit-algorithms --test snapshots
